      "side": 1,
      "message": "Nothing changed on the GSC side except the name of the function. I didn\u0027t change the wire format on GSC. I just made the function name on GSC reflect what is actually happening.\n\nNormally we use BE encoding for TPM commands, but none of us caught that we actually encoded using LE for this ccd info response from ti50.\n\nThis flags bug has existed on main for months. This seems like the best way to fix the issue instead of change the encoding on the wire. Thoughts?",
